vscode: terminal panel, run, select, copy, click, paste
open: report.md

@brief
Eight times: put the first three lines of `sales.csv` at the end of the
report, straight from the shell. Do not open the CSV — changing it fails
the check.

@keys
| `:$r !cmd` | insert the output at the end of the file |
| `head -3 file` | the first three lines |

@hints
`$` in front of `r` is the same `$` as everywhere else: the last line.
--
`:$r !head -3 sales.csv` and Enter.

@solution
    :$r !head -3 sales.csv<Enter>  :wq<Enter>

The reason to drill this one is the habit it replaces. Running the
command in a terminal and copying the output back is four context
switches and a mouse. `:r !` is one command typed where you already are,
and it puts the text exactly where you addressed it rather than wherever
the cursor happened to be when you pasted.

@start report.md
# Daily sales spot check

First three lines of today's export:

@expected report.md
# Daily sales spot check

First three lines of today's export:
id,store,total
ord_1001,aberdeen,42.50
ord_1002,bristol,7.00

@start sales.csv
id,store,total
ord_1001,aberdeen,42.50
ord_1002,bristol,7.00
ord_1003,cardiff,129.99
ord_1004,dundee,8.25
